  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nFor this afternoon, we are monitoring the development of a few \nstrong/severe storms ahead of the cold front, and there continues\nto be a marginal severe risk for damaging wind gusts during peak \nheating over much of the area. Looking ahead, it does appear we \nare nearing the end of the \"dangerous\" heat regime in this long \nand brutally hot summer of 2026. Tomorrow will see the much \nanticipated cold front push through the area, and while the air \nfollowing the front will not be cool and dry enough to remind us \nof fall, it will at least bring conditions that are more typical \nof late September.\n\nFor Tuesday, we could see portions of eastern MS get into the\npicture for a marginal risk for severe storms, but it appears most\nof the activity will stay east of us and will hold off on any\nmessaging for now. Looking ahead for late this week into next \nweekend, as mentioned, drier conditions can be expected with \"less\nhot\" temperatures. Overall, weather impacts will mostly be tied \nto early week heat and convective potential. /EC/",
